## THis is a lightweight host-based intrusion detection agent for linux. 

## ProcWatch
# Overview

ProcWatch is a lightweight Linux process monitoring agent written in C. It scans the /proc filesystem at regular intervals to track active processes and detect changes in the system process list.

## Current Status (Week 1)

This stage implements the core foundation of the agent:

- Reads /proc/[pid]/status for active processes
- Extracts PID and process name
- Polls the system every 500ms

Detects:
- Newly created processes
- Exited processes
- Logs events to standard output
- Runs as a systemd service
- Logs are captured via journald

# Build
gcc proc_scanner.c -o proc_scanner

# Install binary:

sudo mv proc_scanner /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/proc_scanner

# Notes
Uses polling-based monitoring of /proc
Maintains in-memory snapshots of process state
Compares snapshots to detect changes between intervals
Designed for Linux systems only